{
    "background_story": "Greta was a brilliant and fearless oceanographer who spent her life studying the world's oceans. Growing up by the sea, she was always drawn to the mysteries that lay beneath the surface. As a leading expert in underwater exploration, Greta designed and built a state-of-the-art submersible vessel that allowed her to delve deeper into the ocean than anyone before. Her groundbreaking research on marine ecosystems and ocean currents led to numerous discoveries and a deeper understanding of the ocean's role in regulating the Earth's climate. Greta's most notable expedition took her to the Mariana Trench, where she became the first person to submerge to the lowest point on Earth, collecting vital data and samples that shed new light on the ocean's unknown regions.",
